---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="Infrastructure & Network Engineering Services | revs412" description="Independent network infrastructure, secure remote access, systems administration, automation, deployment, troubleshooting, backup and recovery, and technical documentation for remote clients from Morocco." alternatePath="services">
  <main class="shell page services-page">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">remote / Morocco</p>
      <h1>Network infrastructure, secure access, and technical operations.</h1>
      <p>Independent technical work for teams that need dependable infrastructure, secure remote access, practical automation, recovery planning, and documentation that stays useful after handover.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="services-grid" aria-label="Technical service areas">
      <article class="service-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / secure access</p>
        <h2>Network infrastructure and secure remote access</h2>
        <p>Network design, WireGuard access workflows, OpenWrt administration, private service boundaries, and practical troubleshooting for systems that need to remain reachable and controlled.</p>
        <nav class="service-links" aria-label="Related secure access work"><a href={`${base}work/wireguard-admin-access-manager/`}>WireGuard admin access manager →</a><a href={`${base}notes/wireguard-remote-access-setup/`}>WireGuard remote access setup →</a><a href={`${base}notes/openwrt-home-network-setup/`}>OpenWrt network setup →</a></nav>
      </article>

      <article class="service-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / systems operations</p>
        <h2>Systems administration, automation, and recovery</h2>
        <p>Linux and self-hosted services, repeatable deployment workflows, backup replication, and recovery planning that keep operational systems dependable over time.</p>
        <nav class="service-links" aria-label="Related systems operations work"><a href={`${base}notes/docker-deployment-scripts-for-small-services/`}>Docker deployment scripts →</a><a href={`${base}notes/pull-based-backup-replication-to-openwrt-storage/`}>Backup replication to OpenWrt storage →</a><a href={`${base}notes/openwrt-storage-expansion-on-raspberry-pi/`}>OpenWrt storage expansion →</a></nav>
      </article>

      <article class="service-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / technical delivery</p>
        <h2>Troubleshooting and technical documentation</h2>
        <p>Technical investigation, clear operational documentation, and recovery direction that turn implementation details into decisions teams can use and support.</p>
        <nav class="service-links" aria-label="Related technical delivery work"><a href={`${base}work/client-facing-technical-documentation/`}>Client-facing technical documentation →</a><a href={`${base}work/dvr-remote-camera-access-setup/`}>DVR remote camera access setup →</a><a href={`${base}notes/router-firmware-recovery-through-serial-and-flash-access/`}>Router firmware recovery →</a></nav>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="services-contact" aria-labelledby="services-contact-heading">
      <h2 id="services-contact-heading">Discuss a technical project</h2>
      <p>Available for considered infrastructure, network, systems administration, automation, deployment, recovery, and documentation work.</p>
      <a href={`${base}contact/`}>Open a conversation →</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
